"@type":"isbn","#text":"0415149436 (vol 2. : hardcover : alk. paper)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^96003293^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"187467973"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HB99.7 .S43 1997x"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990071711520203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"007171152"}},"processingDate":"2025-12-09T13:02Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"960126"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20020606"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990071711520203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.8 using\n\t\t\t\t\tMARC21slim_MODS3-8_XSL2-0.xsl (Revision 2.79 2025/03/28)"}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Money, markets and method ","subTitle":"essays in honor of Robert W. Clower "},"name":[{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Howitt, Peter,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1946-"}]},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"De Antoni, Elisabetta."},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Leijonhufvud, Axel"},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Clower, Robert W."}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"gnd","#text":"Aufsatzsammlung."},{"@authority":"gnd","#text":"Festschrift."}],"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Northampton, MA "}}],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Edward Elgar"},"dateIssued":"1999"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xvi, 279 p. ; 24 cm."},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Robert W. Clower has had a profound effect on the theory and practice of economics. The distinguished group of contributors to this book celebrates his seminal contribution to economic methodology and theory by providing key accounts of important themes in the area of money, markets and method."},"tableOfContents":[{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Clower's intellectual voyage: the 'Ariadne's thread' of continuity through changes / Elisabetta de Antoni -- Microfoundations: adaptive or optimizing? / Axel Leijonhufvud -- Clower on axiomatics / Lionello F. Punzo -- New tools for making economics an inductive science / Kumaraswamy Velupillai -- From Keynes to Hicks -- an aberration? IS-LM and the analytical nucleus of the general theory / Ingo Barens -- Variations on a two-interest-rate theme / David Laidler -- Thick markets and thin theories: R.W. Clower and the economics of J.M. Keynes / Maria Cristina Marcuzzo -- Price formation and exchange in thin markets: a laboratory comparison of institutions."},{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Timothy N. Cason, Daniel Friedman -- Conformism and multiple sycophantic equilibria / Jean-Pascal Benassy -- Asymmetric contests: a resolution of the Tullock paradox / John G. Riley -- The institutional foundations of the multiplier process / Peter Howitt -- Learning the stock-flow model / David K. Levine -- Price setting in a schematic model of inductive learning / Daniel Heymann, Roberto P.J. Perazzo, Andres R. Schuschny."}],"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"edited by Peter Howitt, Elisabetta de Antoni, Axel Leijonhufvud."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Money"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Capital market"},{"@authority":"gnd","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Keynes, John Maynard",{"@type":"date","#text":"1883-1946"}]},"titleInfo":{"title":"General theory of employment, interest and money"}},{"@authority":"swd","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Keynes, John Maynard."},"titleInfo":{"title":"General theory of employment, interest and money"}}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HG220.A2 M584 1999"},{"@edition":"21","@authority":"ddc","#text":"332"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1858989019"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^^98029677^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"39347310"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990079655870203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HG220.A2 M584 1999"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990079655870203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"007965587"}},"processingDate":"2026-07-30T04:23Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"980616"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20020606"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990079655870203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.8 using\n\t\t\t\t\tMARC21slim_MODS3-8_XSL2-0.xsl (Revision 2.79 2025/03/28)"}},{"titleInfo":{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"economics of Keynes in historical context","subTitle":"an intellectual history of the General Theory"},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Lawlor, Michael S.","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},"originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Basingstoke [England]"}},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","dateIssued":"2006","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xvi, 357 p. : ill. ; 23 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Review","#text":"\"This book offers a comprehensive treatment of the development of Keynes's economic ideas in the General Theory of Employment, Interest and Money. It is the first such exclusively economic theory treatment of Keynes's career since his Collected Works was published, and his papers opened to the public. It uses that material, the historical record of the economics of Keynes's time and place and the scholarship available on Keynes's biography and philosophy to build a narrative of his ideas on economic theory from before World War I - when he was lecturing on economics at Cambridge - through the General Theory in 1936. The predominant early influence is Marshall, and Keynes's Marshallian roots are explored in detail.\"--Jacket."},"tableOfContents":"Introductory material: motivation, methodology and overview -- pt. I. Keynes, Cambridge and the economics of employment -- pt. II. A philosopher and a speculator -- pt. III. \"Shifting equilibria\" in a monetary economy -- Conclusion: a theory of a monetary economy.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Michael S. Lawlor."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 333-344) and i